# GPU and eval workflow

## Preflight (before any VLM / Habitat / Robocasa GPU job)

```bash
uv run emet eval status                # see free VRAM + compute apps
uv run emet eval kill-stale
NEED_MIB=12000 uv run emet eval wait   # or: uv run emet eval check
```

Canonical CLI: **`emet eval {status,check,wait,kill-stale}`**. Bash [`scripts/gpu_preflight.sh`](../../scripts/gpu_preflight.sh) delegates to it (also provides `emet_export_pytorch_alloc` and **`emet_pytest_no_sim_ignore_args`** when sourced). Prefer `emet eval` over raw `pkill` / ad-hoc kills. Verify with `uv run emet eval --help` before suggesting flags. (The `emet eval diagnose` subcommand + `emet jobs` progress/ETA live on the eval branch `exp/agentic-hmeqa-*`, not here — do not suggest them on this branch until merged.)

### Empty `nvidia-smi` is not proof of safety

- Free VRAM / no compute apps does **not** mean Habitat Magnum EGL can create a `WindowlessContext`.
- HM-EQA can fail every episode with `unable to find CUDA device 0 among N EGL devices` while the GPU looks idle (seen 2026-07-24).
- Empty `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` hides the GPU from Torch/Habitat even when `nvidia-smi` still shows the card.
- After a hard kill of Habitat mid-episode, driver/EGL can stay wedged until settle or reboot — use **`emet jobs cancel`**, not raw `kill -9` on `emet-habitat`.

## Experiment reliability

- New eval/sim `Popen` paths must use [`emet.utils.process_tree`](../../src/emet/utils/process_tree.py) (`popen_session` + `terminate_process_tree` / `kill_process_tree`) so timeouts reap GPU grandchildren (`uv` wrappers, mujoco/habitat workers).
- Do **not** run `emet eval kill-stale` from inside a long-running smoke that must stay alive (e.g. `run_dynagraph_dynamic_*`) — use `emet eval wait` only. Set `EMET_GPU_PROTECT_PIDS` if an orchestrator must keep a worker across cleanup.
- After failed/hung evals: `uv run emet eval status`, then check **`~/runs/emet/`**, **`~/.cache/habitat_eqa/results/`**, and per-step logs before re-launching.
- Track / manage long jobs with **`uv run emet jobs`** (list/cancel/logs) and prefer **`emet jobs run --name … -- CMD`** so queue state is visible; registry under `~/runs/emet/jobs/`.
- Docs: [`docs/evaluation.md`](../../docs/evaluation.md), orphan section in [`docs/known_issues.md`](../../docs/known_issues.md).

## One GPU job at a time

Do **not** stack in one uninterrupted session:

- Robocasa dynagraph explore (track 4)
- Full `pytest src/test -m "not sim"` without ignore list
- Habitat HM-EQA with Qwen3-VL-8B
- `run_overnight_eval_smoke.sh`

That sequence caused full-system freezes on an RTX 4090 workstation (GUI + SSH unresponsive; mouse still moved).

| Orchestrator | Default | Notes |
|--------------|---------|-------|
| `run_simulation_smoke_battery.sh` | sequential | **Paper-facing** seven-track battery — see `docs/simulation_testing_plan.md` |
| `run_overnight_cross_track_smoke.sh` | `RUN_DEEP_EVAL=0` | Extended overnight + tier 0 + safe pytest |
| `run_overnight_eval_smoke.sh` | separate night | HM-EQA + OVMM + SQA3D matrix |
| `run_overnight_habitat_eval.sh` | `--resume` | Multi-phase HM-EQA subsets |

## Cursor agent sessions (segfaults)

**"Cursor keeps crashing" here is usually not a busy GPU.** Two distinct modes (see [`docs/known_issues.md`](../../docs/known_issues.md)):

- **Mode A — episode `libcuda` SIGSEGV (`exit=139`):** `emet-habitat run-episode` dies during Qwen3-VL vision generate while Habitat-Sim EGL shares the GPU. Orchestrator logs `FAIL … exit=139` / `dumped core`; kernel shows `python[…]: segfault … in libcuda.so`. The per-qid jsonl is **empty** — that is a crash, not a scored miss. Hot scenes: q104/q105 (`yogvKWUrdnw`), flaky q68.
- **Mode B — agent / `emet` null-IP SIGSEGV:** the Cursor agent process itself dies (`emet[…]: segfault at 0`, or `trap invalid opcode`) when a turn runs or probes Habitat / tears down a GPU context. A detached `emet jobs` / `nohup` child often keeps running.

Rules:

- Launch Habitat / HM-EQA / overnight scripts **only** via **`uv run emet jobs run --name … -- CMD`**, **`nohup … &`**, or a dedicated terminal — never as blocking inline agent shell commands that load Habitat or tear down GPU contexts.
- Do **not** run "quick" Habitat smoke episodes inside the agent turn to "verify EGL", then `kill` them — hard mid-episode kills precede the next `emet` segfault.
- H2H scripts abort after consecutive EGL failures (`EGL_FAIL_ABORT`, default 2) and after a fatal native signal (`NATIVE_CRASH_ABORT`, default 1, writes `native_crash_*.log`) instead of burning the full failset.
- After a crash: `sudo dmesg -T | rg 'segfault|invalid opcode|libcuda'` · `uv run emet eval status` · `uv run emet jobs` · check **`~/runs/emet/`**, **`~/.cache/habitat_eqa/results/`**, **`/tmp/unified_smoke_*.log`** — the detached job may still be running or only half-started.
- Tier 0 + tracks 1–3 PR smoke: see [`docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md`](../../docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md).

## Cross-track smoke entrypoint

```bash
nohup ./scripts/run_overnight_cross_track_smoke.sh \
  >> ~/runs/emet/overnight_cross_track/nohup.log 2>&1 &
tail -f ~/runs/emet/overnight_cross_track/cross_track_*/summary.txt
```

## Unified config smoke (post–PR #68)

When touching config loader or `configs/emet/default.yaml`:

```bash
uv run emet test src/test/config/ -q
uv run python -c "
from emet.core.parameters import get_parameters
p = get_parameters('dynav_innate_mars.yaml')
assert str(p.get('depth_source')).lower() == 'auto'
"
```

See [`docs/emet_config.md`](../../docs/emet_config.md).
